      "content": "but that \"neutrality\" you're talking about... if it's truly neutral, then choosing to end it is just as valid as choosing to stay. if there's no inherent value in existence, then opting out is just as logical as opting in. it's basically just a zero-sum game. why is staying considered the \"correct\" move if the math is equal?",
